Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 40 CLINICAL DATA  High grade infiltrating ductal carcinoma on needle biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  90   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  10  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL 2  EXCISION  UNREMARKABLE FAT  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL 1  EXCISION  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN 2 OF 20 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODE  LEVEL 1    REMOVED_CASE_ID   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODE  LEVEL 1   121  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  NOTE  In the specimen from the breast  lymphatic and blood vessel invasion is not seen and the margins appear free of the tumor  In the right axillary lymph nodes  both metastatic foci measure more than 0 2cm in greatest dimension in tissue section  The malignant cells transgress the capsule of one lymph node  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 21                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are five parts  Labeled  right breast mass   is a 122 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  The external surface is grossly unremarkable and inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a central gray white  firm to rubbery  centrally cystic mass REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  extending to within 0 4cm of an inked margin  The remaining breast tissue are strands of white pink fibrous septae in unremarkable yellow fibroadipose tissue  No other suspicious nodules are identified in the specimen  Representative sections of the tumor with margin are submitted in cassettes A through I  Representative sections of breast tissue are submitted in cassettes J through O  Labeled  right axillary lymph nodes  level 2   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue containing several rubbery nodules  in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Representative tissue is submitted in cassettes P through R  Labeled  axillary lymph nodes  level 1   is a mass of adipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes and several detached lymph node fragments  the mass of fibroadipose tissue is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and remaining aggregate of lymph nodes is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes S through W  Labeled  axillary lymph node  level 1   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a single fragment of fibroadipose tissue containing a lymph node  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  Specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in cassettes X and Y  Labeled  axillary lymph node  level 1  121   is a single pink tan  rubbery nodule REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette Z  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  Irene Kuter  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL 2  EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL 1  EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODE  LEVEL 1    REMOVED_CASE_ID   EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE  LEVEL 1   121  EXCISION , Yes.
