s of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm stellate  firm  tan white mass with gritty cut surface  extending to 0 9cm from the deep margin  and less than 0 5cm from the closest anterior soft tissue resection margin  adjacent to the skin   No frozen section is done  SECTION CODE A  Tumor and closest posterior soft tissue resection margin  B  Tumor and closest anterior soft tissue resection margin  contiguous section with that in A   C  Additional sections of tumor and anterior soft tissue resection margin  D  Additional representative section of the tumor and adjacent posterior soft tissue resection margin  contiguous to the section in C   E  Additional representative section of the tumor adjacent to the anterior margin  F  Additional representative section of the posterior soft tissue resection margin and along the lateral soft tissue resection margin  overinked yellow   Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST   HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  NO FROZEN SECTION DONE  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION , Yes.
